# Every file this repository ever checks with a strict line-oriented parser
# (shell's IFS `read`, `grep -Fxq`, systemd units, PEM, SQL, TSV data) has to
# be LF in the working tree no matter which OS clones it, or those parsers
# fail closed against a trailing \r that isn't part of the value being
# checked. `text=auto` keeps binary detection exactly as before; `eol=lf`
# only overrides what core.autocrlf would otherwise do to whatever git
# already classifies as text, so tracked binaries (png/woff2/etc.) are
# unaffected.
* text=auto eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*Dockerfile text eol=lf
*Caddyfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.tsv text eol=lf
